WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.880
A microphone sealed in a healthy ear canal can record sound that the cochlea made.

2
00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:11.380
What does that returning sound tell us about the amplifier?

3
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.080
And what does it leave out?

4
00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:15.460
Kemp studied human ears.

5
00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:18.580
He delivered brief impulses to the closed canal.

6
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:23.120
After five milliseconds, a slowly decaying component remained.

7
00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:27.440
In the ears with cochlear deafness that were tested, it was absent.

8
00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:29.640
That supports a cochlear source.

9
00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:31.680
It does not identify a motor.

10
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:35.640
Outer hair cells shorten and lengthen with voltage.

11
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.240
The protein prestin is the motor.

12
00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:40.040
Now think about speed.

13
00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:46.040
A tone at 20 kHz, near the top of the human range, completes a cycle every 50

14
00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:51.600
microseconds. Prestin responds to voltage, without burning ATP each cycle.

15
00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:54.560
Membrane filtering and motor speed still matter.

16
00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:57.260
High frequency power remains debated.

17
00:00:58.183 --> 00:01:00.843
How do you connect that protein to an electrical response?

18
00:01:01.563 --> 00:01:03.843
One answer is non -linear capacitance.

19
00:01:04.263 --> 00:01:09.163
In whole -cell voltage clamp, a cell with prestin shows a bell -shaped capacitance.

20
00:01:09.763 --> 00:01:11.043
It peaks at one voltage.

21
00:01:11.663 --> 00:01:15.443
The usual reading is that it reports voltage -dependent movement of charge in the

22
00:01:15.443 --> 00:01:16.443
protein.

23
00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:18.647
A minimal model has two states.

24
00:01:19.267 --> 00:01:22.247
Depolarization shifts prestin toward a contracted state.

25
00:01:22.947 --> 00:01:26.067
Butan and colleagues fitted gerbil prestin in a cell line.

26
00:01:26.747 --> 00:01:32.347
Half activation was at minus −112 mV, with an effective charge of 0 .7.

27
00:01:32.867 --> 00:01:37.507
At that voltage, half the protein is contracted, and capacitance is at its peak.

28
00:01:38.207 --> 00:01:42.707
50 mV more positive, occupancy rises to about 0 .8.

29
00:01:43.447 --> 00:01:46.407
Capacitance falls to about 64% % of the peak.

30
00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:51.050
This is charge movement in a cell line, under stated assumptions.

31
00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:55.330
It does not say how much force or power a hair cell produces.

32
00:01:56.090 --> 00:02:00.870
The structures show purified protein under chosen anion or drug conditions.

33
00:02:01.610 --> 00:02:06.730
The human structures in chloride and salicylate differ by about 200 square

34
00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:09.310
angstroms. That compares two structures.

35
00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:12.090
It is not a stroke measured in a hair cell.

36
00:02:12.850 --> 00:02:16.730
Each answer comes from a different preparation, and none of them is complete.

37
00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:20.030
The returning sound supports a cochlear source.

38
00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:22.910
The capacitance curve reports charge movement.

39
00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:27.110
The structures show purified protein under chosen conditions.

40
00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:31.030
Read them as complementary views, not one settled movie.
